  "interpretation": [
    "The checked self-setter succeeded and every measured output thread policy requested USER_INTERACTIVE (33). The measurement still reproduced the warmed cadence collapse.",
    "Final-minute output was 31.12 versus 30.15 sends/s; output CPU was 20.64 versus 21.04 ms. This is insufficient to qualify a sustained cadence fix.",
    "Both runs started with fair thermal state and reported serious after 60 seconds; scalar thermal categories do not establish matched temperature, CPU frequency or causality.",
    "The trial changes only dedicated-output QoS intent. It does not change capture cadence, profile, rectangles, codec arguments, codec archives, framebuffer ownership or viewer.",
    "The trial was not promoted. A second control run was not needed because the candidate still failed the sustained cadence gate."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Only send_thread_cpu_ms measures CPU time; it covers the whole sending thread between hooks, not just JPEG.",
    "send_wall_minus_thread_cpu_ms includes waiting/descheduling and small endpoint overhead; it does not distinguish their causes.",
    "Requested pthread QoS excludes overrides; raw Mach priority fields identify neither effective QoS nor CPU core or frequency.",
    "Nested stage durations overlap; do not add update/callback/preparation totals to their components.",
    "Source dirty count is the CARenderServer display counter, not the Safari animation sequence.",
    "Thermal state is categorical and sampled once per ten-second window, not a temperature measurement.",
    "Weighted means combine the rounded means in the source report; percentiles are not averaged."
  ],
